            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0808" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-08T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 9—7:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. Peking Government has for the time being virtually ceased to function;
                    Premier is still in Tientsin, his position unchanged. The <pb facs="0809"
                        n="689" xml:id="pg689"/> Minister of Communications is in Tientsin or Mukden
                    plotting in Fengtien-Chihli dispute. Minister of Education refused to assume
                    that office on account of financial difficulties of his Ministry. Minister of
                    War is at Mukden intriguing for the support of Chang Tso-lin to secure
                    Premiership; Minister and Vice Minister of Finance have tendered resignations
                    and gone to Tientsin, and Ministry of Finance is practically non-operative. See
                    my 86, March 8, 1 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d425-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
